<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Censorate</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Censorate was a Chinese government agency responsible for monitoring the conduct of officials and reporting misconduct to the emperor. Its origins lie in the supervisory offices of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han Dynasty</a>. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty</a> it independently monitored officials as part of a system of checks within the central government.</p></div>
